35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Wow, I found some cool stuff! The city is super easy to get around with trains every few minutes! But the ferry is a bit tricky since the last one leaves at 16:20. That's like a puzzle!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"A puzzle is one way to put it, Rin. I call it a waste of time. Two full days spent just getting there and back is an absurd tax on our holiday. We need to be very careful about this.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"My research shows that offshore houses are priced per building, averaging 5,400 yen per person per night, excluding food. This creates a risk if the final headcount changes, as the total cost remains fixed.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"The facilities are a disaster. Some of these places have one bathroom for everyone and the water goes cold. Plus, being stuck on futons in one big room with a strict meal schedule sounds like a nightmare.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"I have found that the lack of personal space can be a significant issue. In a shared house, there was nowhere to go for a moment of solitude, whereas an urban environment naturally provides that balance.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, that sounds scary! If the price is for the whole building, does that mean we might have to pay more if someone can't come? I hate it when the bill changes at the end!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, exactly. It's the same logic as the travel time; we're paying a premium for a lack of flexibility. If we're spending two days in transit and then paying for empty beds, we're not on a holiday—we're on a logistical exercise.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, yes, that is precisely the risk. When a house is let as a whole, the cost is fixed regardless of attendance. This often leads to a situation where the remaining members quietly cover the deficit, which is an unfair arrangement.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, the money is one thing, but look at the living conditions! If we're all crammed into one room on futons with a strict schedule and cold water, we're going to be miserable. We need a place with actual rooms and flexibility.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, I agree. The combination of a rigid timetable and a single shared room removes any possibility of individual decompression. If we cannot find a way to step away from the group, the collective experience becomes draining rather than refreshing.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Takumi, @Toshio, you're making it sound like a scary camp! But if we go to the city, we can have our own space and the trains are so fast! @Asuka, is there a way to know the total cost for everything right now?","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Toshio"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, the city is looking more attractive by the second, mostly because I'm not interested in spending my limited time off staring at a ferry schedule. If we can avoid the transit tax, we might actually come home feeling rested.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, it is impossible to know the total cost now because food is a variable. My research shows that all-in rates force everyone to pay the same regardless of appetite, whereas separate payments are more precise and fair.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, forget the appetite for a second. The real problem is the structure. If we're forced into a rigid schedule with no privacy and bad bathrooms, the ""fairness"" of the bill won't matter because we'll all be exhausted and grumpy. We need a place with actual doors.","{""words"":47,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, you are correct. The absence of physical boundaries and the imposition of a strict schedule create a psychological pressure that is difficult to ignore. A city environment offers the autonomy we need to maintain our well-being.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, I don't like that the food cost is a secret! I want to know exactly how much money I need to save so there are no surprises later. But the city sounds like a win-win! Let's pick the easiest one!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, ""easiest"" is a start, but let's be precise: we want the option that minimizes the time spent waiting and moving. If the city saves us two days of transit, it's the only rational choice. I'm ready for the options.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I agree that the city is a strong candidate. However, regardless of the location, we must ensure the payment system is transparent. I will support the option that avoids fixed-cost risks and allows for precise, individual settlement of expenses.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Takumi,,I'm with you all. The city is the only way to go. I can't deal with cold water and no privacy for a whole week. Let's just make sure we have actual rooms and no strict schedules. I'm ready.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I agree. The data suggests that a city environment provides the necessary balance of shared time and personal autonomy. Avoiding the constraints of a single room and a rigid schedule is essential for a sustainable trip. I am ready to see the options.,"{""words"":43,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
