60,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Option C sounds the best! We can use those fast trains, and since we have separate rooms, it won't be a scary camp! But @Asuka, will we know the total cost for everything before we go?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, stop worrying about the total cost for a moment and look at the clock. Option A is a non-starter; I refuse to sacrifice two days of my life to a ferry schedule. Option C is the only rational choice for efficiency.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, we cannot know the exact total in advance because individual choices vary. However, Option C is the most equitable. Separate accommodation and loose plans eliminate the risk of fixed-cost deficits and unfair subsidies.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"Option C is the only one that makes sense. Option A is a nightmare with that one bathroom and no privacy, and Option B still has those strict inn schedules. I need a door and my own space. I vote C.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option C is the most logical choice. It provides the physical and psychological boundaries necessary to prevent the feeling of being crowded, while the urban environment allows for the solitude I found lacking in previous years. I vote C.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, I'm still a little worried about the surprises, but if Option C means no one has to pay for someone else's bed, then it's the fairest! Plus, it sounds like a big city adventure! I vote C!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, for once, your ""adventure"" actually aligns with logic. Option C eliminates the transit tax and the rigid scheduling of the other two. It's the only way to ensure we don't return home needing another holiday. I vote C.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"I agree. Option C is the only choice that ensures financial transparency. By arranging our own accommodation and routes, we avoid the risk of a shared deficit and ensure that each person pays exactly for what they use. I vote C.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"I've already said it, but I'm sticking with C. I can't risk another trip where I'm counting the days until I can go home. No strict mealtimes and no shared futons. I vote C.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,The consensus is clear. Option C is the only arrangement that respects both our collective time and our individual need for space. It is the most sustainable choice for the group. I vote C.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,Yay! Everyone likes Option C! It's going to be a super fun city adventure and I won't have to worry about scary surprise bills at the end! I'm so happy we all agree! I vote C!,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"It's a rare moment of total agreement. Since we've successfully avoided the ferry nightmare and the rigid schedules of an inn, there's no reason to overthink it. I vote C.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"The result is unanimous. Option C is the only choice that removes the risk of hidden costs and ensures a fair, transparent distribution of expenses. I stand by my decision. I vote C.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"I'm glad we're all on the same page. No shared rooms, no cold water, and no strict schedules. This is the only way to make sure the trip is actually a break. I vote C.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"I agree. By prioritizing autonomy and flexibility, we ensure that the trip remains a positive experience for everyone. Option C is the only choice that addresses all our concerns. I vote C.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Rin,,I'm so excited! A big city adventure with no surprises and no scary camps! Let's go make some amazing memories together! I vote C!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Since we've managed to avoid the logistical disaster of a ferry and the suffocating nature of a shared inn, I'm satisfied. Let's just make sure the ""loose plan"" stays loose. I vote C.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Asuka,,The decision is final. Option C is the only responsible choice that guarantees financial transparency and prevents any individual from being unfairly burdened by shared costs. I vote C.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Takumi,,I'm done. Option C is the only way to go if we want to actually enjoy ourselves. No more counting down the days until we leave. I vote C.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I concur. Option C is the only choice that guarantees the necessary balance of togetherness and solitude. It is the most rational decision for the well-being of the group. I vote C.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
